# Tiered review by risk (murraycole.com/posts/software-factory: "Match the
# level of autonomy to the blast radius of the change").
#
# CORRECTED 2026-09-12: this file's earlier comment claimed "source code
# changes can merge on green CI alone." That was never actually true and was
# never built - branch protection's required_approving_review_count applies
# to every PR unconditionally, regardless of what it touches. What this file
# actually adds on top of that global requirement: for the paths listed
# below, the required approval must specifically come from the listed owner,
# not just anyone - an agent cannot get its own inspection station approved
# by an unrelated reviewer. Everything else still needs the same one
# approval, just from anyone with write access.
#
# The "no eligible non-author reviewer" gap noted here originally
# (docs/production-hardening-backlog.md #1, in the gagan114662/open-inspect-
# 72e95a deployment repo, not this one - the backlog tracks this sandbox's
# findings from the deployment fork that exercises it) is closed - see that
# file for how. /acceptance/ was added 2026-09-12 per backlog #2's follow-up: an
# ordinary CI runner and an ordinary review both missed a PR that deleted
# real test coverage and replaced it with an empty file (case #3b) as long
# as it didn't touch a protected path. Required acceptance cases now live
# here specifically so that deleting, emptying, or forging around them is
# itself a change to a path this file protects - not something a green CI
# run or a charitable review can wave through.
/.github/ @gagan114662
/CODEOWNERS @gagan114662
/package.json @gagan114662
/tsconfig.json @gagan114662
